Bitwise Operators:-

Bitwise operators are used to perform operations on the binary (bit) representation of integers. They work bit by bit and return a new integer as the result.

	•	& → Both bits must be 1
	•	| → At least one bit is 1
	•	^ → Bits must be different
	•	~ → Reverse (invert) all bits
	•	<< → Shift bits to the left
	•	>> → Shift bits to the right
